# Story 22: Layout Tree (##pg layout) (40s)
# Hook: See your whole tab at once -- ##pg layout draws the entire structure as a tree.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-022-layout-tree.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
See your whole tab at once -- ##pg layout draws the entire structure as a tree.

[00:04.0 --> 00:16.0]
Start rysh and build something with depth: split right for a column, split down for a row, then stack a pane on top.

[00:16.0 --> 00:28.0]
In rysh mode, ##pg layout prints the full tree: lanes, then groups, then the stacked panes inside them.

[00:28.0 --> 00:36.0]
Pair it with ##pg info to drill into just the group your active pane lives in.

[00:36.0 --> 00:40.0]
One command, the whole picture. ##pg layout is your map of any tab.

